<description>&lt;p&gt;Algeria is deploying troops to Niger for the first foreign mission in over 50 years to protect energy assets, while Nigerian forces face bandit attacks that killed a soldier and prompted calls for more military bases. In Niger, a convoy of Governor Bago crashed, killing four students, a driver and a young lady. ISWAP leader responsible for attacks in Owo, Kogi and Niger was killed in Ondo. Niger accuses Chad of a drone strike that killed two civilians. Overcrowding in a Niger NSCDC detention cell caused the deaths of 14 minors among 33 detainees. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiX0FVX3lxTE9GMDEydnpWYmZSRXVGaHJydENaWTF3Y29hQWdTdlROc2swOVB3UWFrMGttNWpXSWpybnpjVDNlWkJ3VjVhdGFEYXg2X202TkdwSEt0QzNYMjJpZnB0TTM4?oc=5&quot;&gt;Gistmania&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihAFBVV95cUxPSFIwTC1ZYU5UWkZCam83eGFETUpwbjhTNUtkR3hGbHpXYjlBYjhzbzE3Q1lBTE1LZjlXMmJ0RXFFUzZ4VHlxbFhHLWo2MzMwQVMtUjR3TjQ5by0wd3VZUDY1eGF0LWVDMzJEOUd4eUhfVVJyb1pfeGhRYjltS05TZktwQ2g?oc=5&quot;&gt;Edugist&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiowFBVV95cUxPUkFzSlcyTEU5ZjJRWC1EN05mNU0zX0t2bFA0MWQ3YWFQX3ppcGdJeXNibl9MOWoxY2VlWEh0TTVsa25SdzBaak1Dd0xYQ3JvQ1pSN1hNRzhIc1p1aW5iZVdIelBpRHhLV1ZILWVNYklVOUhlZzRpZkplNXVjV1QyVUlJcDlzeF9Mb1ZMbjkzN0xISUlOZlR2bnJxaURzdVF3NDBR?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Sun Nigeria&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMigAFBVV95cUxNcnZSZnd5RHFJZFA2TTkzOXFxUGNVWTN0U1d2ajRSSmtLdHg5ZzFielFhUEJaZVJPNVlrSVFEVWFmeHk5cVZYYWFtVFBfbWpjWnFPZWRObjJzRHQ4dzU2WmZtUklTM1FVTERRX1VoOVVuRDc0N3F2NThjZko1dTM4Vw?oc=